quran[12]{c,v,t}:
  16,15,"And He has cast firm mountains in the earth lest it shakes beneath you. And (He has made) the rivers and pathways, so you may be guided (to reach your destination)."
  16,16,"And (there are) landmarks (to help navigate during the day), and (at night) they are guided by the stars."
  16,17,So can the One Who creates be like the one who cannot create? Will you not then be mindful of advice?
  16,18,"And if you were to count the blessings of Allah, you would never be able to count them. Indeed, Allah is Most-Forgiving, All-Merciful."
  16,19,And Allah knows whatever you hide and whatever you disclose.
  16,20,And those (idols) they worship besides Allah do not create anything and are themselves created.
  16,21,"(They are) dead, not alive, and they are not (even) aware of when they (i.e. their worshippers) will be resurrected."
  16,22,"Your God is (only) One God. Those who do not believe in the Hereafter—their hearts are deniers, and they are arrogant."
  16,23,"There is no doubt that Allah knows whatever they conceal and whatever they reveal. Indeed, He does not like the arrogant."
  16,24,And when it is said to them: ‘What has your Lord revealed?’ They say: ‘Stories of the ancient people.’
  16,25,"(This is so) that, on the Day of Resurrection, they may bear their entire burdens, as well as the burdens of those whom they mislead without knowledge. Beware! Evil is what they bear!"
  16,26,"Those before them had also schemed, but Allah demolished their constructions from the foundation. So the roof collapsed upon them from above, and the punishment overtook them from where they could not perceive."
